    "notes": "After the death of her first husband Herman, Richilde retained Hainaut and married Baldwin VI of Flanders, who ruled Hainaut with her. Their younger son Baldwin II continued the Hainaut line after the loss of Flanders to Robert the Frisian. Richilde's ancestry is disputed in medieval and modern genealogical literature, so father and mother are left blank. Birth estimates vary substantially, including c.1018 and later dates. Her independent/co-regnal status and the exact beginning of her rule are variously dated c.1050 or 1051; she continued as regent/co-ruler for Baldwin II after 1071.",
